  "id": "DrugBank_DB12301 - MONDO_12268",
  "verbalization": "Doravirine is implicated in the treatment of AIDS through a chain of indications that ultimately lead to the condition. The evidence suggests that Doravirine is associated with HIV Infectious Disease, which in turn is linked to AIDS via three distinct pathways: one involving Elvitegravir, another with Zalcitabine, and a third with Enfuvirtide. These pathways highlight the role of HIV Infectious Disease in the progression to AIDS, as each of these drugs is used to manage HIV infection. The shared indication of HIV Infectious Disease across all three paths underscores a common mechanism in the treatment of HIV, which is critical for the development of AIDS. The integration of these pathways supports the notion that Doravirine may contribute to the management of HIV, thereby influencing the progression to AIDS. The evidence is consistent and highlights the importance of HIV treatment in the context of AIDS, reinforcing the role of Doravirine in this broader therapeutic context.",
